IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ucpr-dates`
IMPORT `ucpr-rules`
IMPORT `ucpr-seat`

-- Uniform Civil Procedure Rules 1999 (Qld) -- cases for the claimant's questions (ucpr-seat.l4). Every expected value is
-- worked by hand from the deposited text (the version in force from 29 October 2026) with the rule, and never copied
-- from the encoding's output. Day counts are worked in the comments: the day of the event is not counted (fork F1).
-- Month lengths used: November 30, December 31, January 31, February 28 (29 in 2028), March 31.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the claimant`

§§ `r 24 -- the claim in force and renewal`

-- Filed 15 Mar 2026: in force for 1 year starting that day, so to 14 Mar 2027.
#ASSERT `Until when is my claim in force?` (`the day` 15 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 14 3 2027
-- Filed 1 Jan 2026: to 31 Dec 2026.
#ASSERT `Until when is my claim in force?` (`the day` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `the day` 31 12 2026
-- Filed 29 Feb 2028: the anniversary falls on 28 Feb 2029, so the last day is 27 Feb 2029.
#ASSERT `Until when is my claim in force?` (`the day` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `the day` 27 2 2029

-- Filed 10 Mar 2026; fifth anniversary 10 Mar 2031.
-- First renewal: ends 9 Mar 2027, renewal from 10 Mar 2027 to 9 Mar 2028, all before 10 Mar 2031: no leave.
#ASSERT `Can my claim be renewed?` (`the day` 10 3 2026) (`the day` 9 3 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the registrar may renew it for up to 1 year without the court's leave`
-- Already served: r 24(2) does not apply.
#ASSERT `Can my claim be renewed?` (`the day` 10 3 2026) (`the day` 9 3 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: rule 24(2) renews only a claim not yet served on the defendant`
-- Registrar not satisfied.
#ASSERT `Can my claim be renewed?` (`the day` 10 3 2026) (`the day` 9 3 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the registrar is not satisfied of reasonable efforts to serve or another good reason`
-- Edge: renewal from 10 Mar 2030 to 9 Mar 2031 ends the day before the fifth anniversary: no leave.
#ASSERT `Can my claim be renewed?` (`the day` 10 3 2026) (`the day` 9 3 2030) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the registrar may renew it for up to 1 year without the court's leave`
-- Renewal from 1 Jul 2030 to 30 Jun 2031 crosses 10 Mar 2031: without leave only to 9 Mar 2031.
#ASSERT `Can my claim be renewed?` (`the day` 10 3 2026) (`the day` 30 6 2030) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the registrar may renew it without leave only up to the day before the fifth anniversary; a longer period needs the court's leave`
-- Renewal from 10 Mar 2031, the fifth anniversary itself: all of it needs leave.
#ASSERT `Can my claim be renewed?` (`the day` 10 3 2026) (`the day` 9 3 2031) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `only with the court's leave: the whole renewal period falls on or after the fifth anniversary`

-- r 24(6): the original filing day.
#ASSERT `When is my renewed claim taken to have started?` (`the day` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 10 3 2026

§§ `r 137 and Chapter 9, Part 1 -- notice of intention to defend and default judgment`

-- Served 2 Nov 2026: 28 days -> 30 Nov 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the defendant file a notice of intention to defend?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 30 11 2026
-- Served 15 Dec 2026: 16 days to 31 Dec, 12 more -> 12 Jan 2027 (no Christmas break in these rules).
#ASSERT `By when must the defendant file a notice of intention to defend?` (`the day` 15 12 2026) EQUALS `the day` 12 1 2027

-- Default judgment, claim served 2 Nov 2026, last day for the notice 30 Nov 2026.
-- A request on the last day itself: the time has not ended.
#ASSERT `Can I get default judgment?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 30 11 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE `a debt or liquidated demand` FALSE EQUALS `not yet: the 28 days for a notice of intention to defend have not ended`
-- The day after: a debt -> r 283.
#ASSERT `Can I get default judgment?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 1 12 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE `a debt or liquidated demand` FALSE EQUALS `yes: I can file a request for judgment for not more than the amount claimed, interest and costs, given by a registrar (r 283)`
#ASSERT `Can I get default judgment?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 1 12 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE `unliquidated damages` FALSE EQUALS `yes: I can file a request for judgment conditional on the assessment of damages, and costs (r 284)`
#ASSERT `Can I get default judgment?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 1 12 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE `detention of goods only` FALSE EQUALS `yes: I can file a request for judgment for the return or value of the goods (r 285)`
#ASSERT `Can I get default judgment?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 1 12 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE `recovery of possession of land only` FALSE EQUALS `yes: I can file a request for judgment for possession of the land and costs (r 286)`
#ASSERT `Can I get default judgment?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 1 12 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE `recovery of possession of land only` TRUE EQUALS `no: rule 286 gives no judgment for delivery of possession under a mortgage; I must apply to the court (r 288)`
#ASSERT `Can I get default judgment?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 1 12 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE `two or more of those four kinds and nothing else` FALSE EQUALS `yes: I can request judgment on each claim as if it were my only claim (r 287)`
#ASSERT `Can I get default judgment?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 1 12 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE `any other claim` FALSE EQUALS `I must apply to the court for the judgment it considers justified on the pleadings (r 288)`
-- Service not proved (r 282).
#ASSERT `Can I get default judgment?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 1 12 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE `a debt or liquidated demand` FALSE EQUALS `not yet: I must first prove service of the claim`
-- A late notice filed before the request (r 138).
#ASSERT `Can I get default judgment?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 1 12 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE `a debt or liquidated demand` FALSE EQUALS `no: the defendant has filed a notice of intention to defend`
-- Served interstate: the Commonwealth Act sets the time (r 137(2)).
#ASSERT `Can I get default judgment?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 1 12 2026) TRUE FALSE TRUE `a debt or liquidated demand` FALSE EQUALS `not under these rules: the Service and Execution of Process Act 1992 (Cwlth) sets the time`

-- Fixed costs on a default judgment for a debt.
-- Supreme or District Court: Schedule 1 items 19 and 20, 2123 + 558, plus 100 fees = 2781.
#ASSERT `What fixed costs go on my default judgment?` `the Supreme Court or the District Court` 40000 100 EQUALS JUST 2781
-- Magistrates Court, Schedule 2 Part 2 items 1 and 4. Column A at exactly $2,500: 454.55 + 119.95 = 574.50.
#ASSERT `What fixed costs go on my default judgment?` `a Magistrates Court` 2500 0 EQUALS JUST 574.50
-- One cent over: column B, 858.55 + 200.15 = 1058.70; also at $5,000.
#ASSERT `What fixed costs go on my default judgment?` `a Magistrates Court` 2500.01 0 EQUALS JUST 1058.70
#ASSERT `What fixed costs go on my default judgment?` `a Magistrates Court` 5000 0 EQUALS JUST 1058.70
-- Column C, 1343.00 + 303.40 = 1646.40, at $20,000; plus 50 fees = 1696.40.
#ASSERT `What fixed costs go on my default judgment?` `a Magistrates Court` 20000 50 EQUALS JUST 1696.40
-- Column D, 1491.00 + 333.10 = 1824.10, from $20,000.01 to $50,000.
#ASSERT `What fixed costs go on my default judgment?` `a Magistrates Court` 20000.01 0 EQUALS JUST 1824.10
#ASSERT `What fixed costs go on my default judgment?` `a Magistrates Court` 50000 0 EQUALS JUST 1824.10
-- Over $50,000: Schedule 2 Part 3 fixed cost items 19 and 20, 1698.00 + 446.40 = 2144.40; plus 100 fees = 2244.40.
#ASSERT `What fixed costs go on my default judgment?` `a Magistrates Court` 50000.01 0 EQUALS JUST 2144.40
#ASSERT `What fixed costs go on my default judgment?` `a Magistrates Court` 250000 100 EQUALS JUST 2244.40

§§ `Pleadings and admissions`

-- Defence served 10 Nov 2026: reply within 14 days -> 24 Nov 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I reply?` (`the day` 10 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 24 11 2026
-- Counterclaim served 10 Nov 2026: a party, 14 days -> 24 Nov; not a party, 28 days -> 8 Dec 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I answer the counterclaim?` (`the day` 10 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS `the day` 24 11 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I answer the counterclaim?` (`the day` 10 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS `the day` 8 12 2026
-- Pleadings close: on service of my reply (20 Nov), or 14 days after the defence (24 Nov).
#ASSERT `When do the pleadings close?` (`the day` 10 11 2026) TRUE (`the day` 20 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 20 11 2026
#ASSERT `When do the pleadings close?` (`the day` 10 11 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `the day` 24 11 2026

-- Notice to admit served 1 Oct 2026: 14 days -> 15 Oct 2026.
-- Disputed on the last day.
#ASSERT `Is the other party taken to admit?` (`the day` 1 10 2026) TRUE (`the day` 15 10 2026) (`the day` 20 10 2026) EQUALS `no: the other party served a notice disputing it within 14 days`
-- Disputed a day late.
#ASSERT `Is the other party taken to admit?` (`the day` 1 10 2026) TRUE (`the day` 16 10 2026) (`the day` 20 10 2026) EQUALS `yes: the other party is taken to admit it, for this proceeding only, unless the court gives leave to withdraw`
-- Nothing yet, today the last day.
#ASSERT `Is the other party taken to admit?` (`the day` 1 10 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2000) (`the day` 15 10 2026) EQUALS `not yet: the 14 days for a disputing notice have not ended`
-- Nothing, the day after.
#ASSERT `Is the other party taken to admit?` (`the day` 1 10 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2000) (`the day` 16 10 2026) EQUALS `yes: the other party is taken to admit it, for this proceeding only, unless the court gives leave to withdraw`

§§ `r 214 -- disclosure`

-- Pleadings closed 24 Nov 2026: 6 days to 30 Nov, 22 more -> 22 Dec 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I deliver my list of documents?` (`the day` 24 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`the day` 22 12 2026)
-- An earlier order sets the times: no answer here.
#ASSERT `By when must I deliver my list of documents?` (`the day` 24 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A document found on 5 Jan 2027: 7 days -> 12 Jan 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I disclose a later document?` (`the day` 5 1 2027) EQUALS `the day` 12 1 2027
-- Copies asked for on 25 Dec 2026: 6 days to 31 Dec, 8 more -> 8 Jan 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I deliver requested copies?` (`the day` 25 12 2026) EQUALS `the day` 8 1 2027

§§ `Chapter 14, Part 2 -- personal injury statements`

#ASSERT `Must I serve a statement of loss and damage?` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Part 2 of Chapter 14 does not apply: the proceeding is not for damages for personal injury or death`
#ASSERT `Must I serve a statement of loss and damage?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no further statement is needed: compliance with Part 2 was waived by written notice (r 546)`
#ASSERT `Must I serve a statement of loss and damage?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `serve it within 28 days after the close of pleadings, and before any request for trial date is filed`

-- Pleadings closed 24 Nov 2026 -> 22 Dec 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I serve my statement of loss and damage?` (`the day` 24 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 22 12 2026
-- My statement served 22 Dec 2026: 9 days to 31 Dec, 19 more -> 19 Jan 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must the defendant serve its statement?` (`the day` 22 12 2026) EQUALS `the day` 19 1 2027

-- The chain (rr 547, 550). Pleadings closed 1 Feb 2027. 28 days -> 1 Mar 2027 (February 2027 has 28 days).
-- Mine on 1 Mar 2027 (day 28) and theirs on 29 Mar 2027 (28 days after mine): both in time.
#ASSERT `Were the statements served in time?` (`the day` 1 2 2027) (`the day` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`the day` 29 3 2027) (`the day` 1 4 2027) EQUALS `both statements were served in time`
-- Theirs on 30 Mar 2027, a day late.
#ASSERT `Were the statements served in time?` (`the day` 1 2 2027) (`the day` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`the day` 30 3 2027) (`the day` 1 4 2027) EQUALS `the defendant was late with its statement of expert and economic evidence`
-- Mine on 2 Mar 2027, day 29: late.
#ASSERT `Were the statements served in time?` (`the day` 1 2 2027) (`the day` 2 3 2027) TRUE (`the day` 29 3 2027) (`the day` 1 4 2027) EQUALS `I was late with my statement of loss and damage`
-- Theirs not served; today 29 Mar 2027, their last day: still running.
#ASSERT `Were the statements served in time?` (`the day` 1 2 2027) (`the day` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2000) (`the day` 29 3 2027) EQUALS `my statement was in time and the defendant's 28 days are still running`
-- Theirs not served; today 30 Mar 2027: late.
#ASSERT `Were the statements served in time?` (`the day` 1 2 2027) (`the day` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2000) (`the day` 30 3 2027) EQUALS `the defendant was late with its statement of expert and economic evidence`

-- Assessment set for 30 Nov 2026: mine at least 21 days before -> 9 Nov 2026; theirs 7 days before -> 23 Nov 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I serve my statement before the assessment?` (`the day` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 9 11 2026
#ASSERT `By when must the defendant serve its statement before the assessment?` (`the day` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 23 11 2026

§§ `rr 98, 359 -- a claimant under a legal incapacity`

#ASSERT `Is my settlement binding on me?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my settlement binding on me?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my settlement binding on me?` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `rr 303, 304, 307 -- discontinuance`

#ASSERT `Can I discontinue without leave?` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I can discontinue by filing a notice and serving it on the other parties`
#ASSERT `Can I discontinue without leave?` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only with the court's leave or the consent of the other parties`
#ASSERT `Can I discontinue without leave?` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `only with the court's leave or the consent of the other parties`
#ASSERT `Can I discontinue without leave?` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `only with the court's leave or the consent of the other parties`
#ASSERT `Can I discontinue without leave?` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only with the court's leave, because I represent another person`
#ASSERT `What costs if I discontinue?` FALSE EQUALS `I must pay the defendant's costs up to the discontinuance and any costs it causes another party`
#ASSERT `What costs if I discontinue?` TRUE EQUALS `whatever costs order the court considers appropriate`

§§ `Chapter 9, Part 5 -- offers to settle`

-- Served 2 Nov 2026: open at least to 16 Nov 2026.
#ASSERT `What is the earliest closing day for my offer?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 16 11 2026

-- Closing day 16 Nov 2026.
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my offer?` (`the day` 16 11 2026) (`the day` 16 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS `no: not while it is open, without the court's leave`
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my offer?` (`the day` 16 11 2026) (`the day` 16 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS `yes, with the court's leave, though it can still be accepted until the application is decided`
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my offer?` (`the day` 16 11 2026) (`the day` 17 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS `there is nothing to withdraw: the offer lapsed at the end of its period`

#ASSERT `Can I accept the offer?` (`the day` 16 11 2026) (`the day` 16 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I accept the offer?` (`the day` 16 11 2026) (`the day` 17 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I accept the offer?` (`the day` 16 11 2026) (`the day` 10 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Costs. My offer of $100,000, not accepted, court satisfied.
-- Judgment exactly $100,000: "no less favourable" -> r 360.
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `I made the offer to the defendant` FALSE FALSE 100000 100000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the defendant must pay my costs: standard basis up to and including the day the offer was served, indemnity basis after it (r 360)`
-- One cent under: r 360 does not apply.
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `I made the offer to the defendant` FALSE FALSE 100000 99999.99 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the offer rules do not apply: costs are in the court's discretion and follow the event unless it orders otherwise (r 681)`
-- Beaten, but the defendant shows another order is appropriate.
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `I made the offer to the defendant` FALSE FALSE 100000 120000 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the court decides: the defendant has shown another costs order is appropriate (r 360(2))`
-- Accepted; or the court not satisfied I was willing and able.
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `I made the offer to the defendant` TRUE FALSE 100000 120000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the offer rules do not apply: costs are in the court's discretion and follow the event unless it orders otherwise (r 681)`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `I made the offer to the defendant` FALSE FALSE 100000 120000 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the offer rules do not apply: costs are in the court's discretion and follow the event unless it orders otherwise (r 681)`
-- The defendant's offer of $100,000. Judgment one cent under: r 361(2).
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `the defendant made the offer to me` FALSE FALSE 100000 99999.99 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the defendant pays my standard costs up to and including the day of service; I pay its indemnity costs after it and get none of mine after it (r 361(2))`
-- Judgment exactly equal: not "less favourable", so r 361 does not apply (finding 4).
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `the defendant made the offer to me` FALSE FALSE 100000 100000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the offer rules do not apply: costs are in the court's discretion and follow the event unless it orders otherwise (r 681)`
-- Served at trial, judgment $50,000: r 361(3).
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `the defendant made the offer to me` FALSE FALSE 100000 50000 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I get standard costs to the opening of court on the next trial day; the defendant gets its indemnity costs after that (r 361(3))`
-- Not reached, but a party (here I) shows another order is appropriate (r 361(2) "Unless a party shows").
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `the defendant made the offer to me` FALSE FALSE 100000 50000 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the court decides: a party has shown another costs order is appropriate (r 361(2) or r 361A(2))`
-- Dismissed: r 361A; and with another order shown.
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `the defendant made the offer to me` FALSE TRUE 100000 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I must pay the defendant's costs: standard basis up to and including the day the offer was served, indemnity basis after it (r 361A)`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `the defendant made the offer to me` FALSE TRUE 100000 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the court decides: a party has shown another costs order is appropriate (r 361(2) or r 361A(2))`
-- My offer, my claim dismissed: no r 360.
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `I made the offer to the defendant` FALSE TRUE 100000 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the offer rules do not apply: costs are in the court's discretion and follow the event unless it orders otherwise (r 681)`

§§ `r 389 -- delay`

-- Last step 1 Mar 2025; first anniversary 1 Mar 2026, second 1 Mar 2027.
#ASSERT `What must I do before my next step?` (`the day` 1 3 2025) (`the day` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `no notice or order needed: a year has not passed without a step`
#ASSERT `What must I do before my next step?` (`the day` 1 3 2025) (`the day` 2 3 2026) EQUALS `I must first give every other party a month's notice of my intention to proceed`
#ASSERT `What must I do before my next step?` (`the day` 1 3 2025) (`the day` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `I must first give every other party a month's notice of my intention to proceed`
#ASSERT `What must I do before my next step?` (`the day` 1 3 2025) (`the day` 2 3 2027) EQUALS `I need the court's order before taking a new step`
-- Last step 29 Feb 2024: anniversary 28 Feb 2025.
#ASSERT `What must I do before my next step?` (`the day` 29 2 2024) (`the day` 28 2 2025) EQUALS `no notice or order needed: a year has not passed without a step`
#ASSERT `What must I do before my next step?` (`the day` 29 2 2024) (`the day` 1 3 2025) EQUALS `I must first give every other party a month's notice of my intention to proceed`

-- A month's notice given 15 Jan 2027: the month ends 15 Feb, step from 16 Feb 2027.
#ASSERT `From when can I take my step after notice?` (`the day` 15 1 2027) EQUALS `the day` 16 2 2027
-- Given 31 Jan 2027: the month ends 28 Feb 2027, step from 1 Mar 2027.
#ASSERT `From when can I take my step after notice?` (`the day` 31 1 2027) EQUALS `the day` 1 3 2027
-- Given 15 Dec 2026: the month ends 15 Jan 2027, step from 16 Jan 2027.
#ASSERT `From when can I take my step after notice?` (`the day` 15 12 2026) EQUALS `the day` 16 1 2027

§§ `rr 514, 515 -- minor claims`

#ASSERT `Do the simplified procedures apply?` 25000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: it is a minor claim, so the simplified procedures apply`
#ASSERT `Do the simplified procedures apply?` 25000.01 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the simplified procedures do not apply`
#ASSERT `Do the simplified procedures apply?` 25000.01 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, to the extent the parties agreed in writing and filed the agreement`
#ASSERT `Do the simplified procedures apply?` 10000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the simplified procedures do not apply`
#ASSERT `Do the simplified procedures apply?` 10000 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the simplified procedures do not apply`

§§ `r 691 and Schedule 2 -- the Magistrates Courts scale`

-- Standard basis: the amount recovered; indemnity basis: the amount claimed.
#ASSERT `Which Magistrates Courts scale column applies?` `the standard basis` 2500 60000 EQUALS `column A ($2,500 or under)`
#ASSERT `Which Magistrates Courts scale column applies?` `the indemnity basis` 2500 60000 EQUALS `Part 3 (over $50,000)`
#ASSERT `Which Magistrates Courts scale column applies?` `the standard basis` 2500.01 0 EQUALS `column B (over $2,500 but not over $5,000)`
#ASSERT `Which Magistrates Courts scale column applies?` `the standard basis` 5000 0 EQUALS `column B (over $2,500 but not over $5,000)`
#ASSERT `Which Magistrates Courts scale column applies?` `the standard basis` 5000.01 0 EQUALS `column C (over $5,000 but not over $20,000)`
#ASSERT `Which Magistrates Courts scale column applies?` `the indemnity basis` 0 20000 EQUALS `column C (over $5,000 but not over $20,000)`
#ASSERT `Which Magistrates Courts scale column applies?` `the indemnity basis` 0 20000.01 EQUALS `column D (over $20,000 but not over $50,000)`
#ASSERT `Which Magistrates Courts scale column applies?` `the standard basis` 50000 0 EQUALS `column D (over $20,000 but not over $50,000)`
#ASSERT `Which Magistrates Courts scale column applies?` `the standard basis` 50000.01 0 EQUALS `Part 3 (over $50,000)`

§§ `r 697 -- suing in a higher court`

#ASSERT `Are my costs cut back for the court I chose?` `a Magistrates Court` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `rule 697 does not reduce my costs`
#ASSERT `Are my costs cut back for the court I chose?` `the Supreme Court or the District Court` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `assessed as if the proceeding had been started in a Magistrates Court, unless the court orders otherwise`
#ASSERT `Are my costs cut back for the court I chose?` `the Supreme Court or the District Court` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `assessed as if the proceeding had been started in the District Court, unless the court orders otherwise`
#ASSERT `Are my costs cut back for the court I chose?` `the Supreme Court or the District Court` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `rule 697 does not reduce my costs`
#ASSERT `Are my costs cut back for the court I chose?` `the Supreme Court or the District Court` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `rule 697 does not reduce my costs`

§§ `r 748 -- appeals`

-- Decision 3 Dec 2026: 28 days -> 31 Dec 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I file my notice of appeal?` (`the day` 3 12 2026) EQUALS `the day` 31 12 2026
-- Decision 5 Feb 2027: 23 days to 28 Feb, 5 more -> 5 Mar 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I file my notice of appeal?` (`the day` 5 2 2027) EQUALS `the day` 5 3 2027

§§ `The duty chain as a trace`

-- rr 547, 550: the plaintiff serves on day 20 after the close of pleadings, the defendant 28 days later (day 48).
#TRACE `rr 547, 550 -- the personal injury statements` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the plaintiff` DOES `serve a statement of loss and damage` AT 20
    PARTY `the defendant` DOES `serve a statement of expert and economic evidence` AT 48
